    "comments": "ugreenhost\nugreenhost\n\n5 years, 4 months ago\nC is right\nMiBol\nMiBol\n\n5 years ago\nA distinction between scalability and elasticity is that elasticity is done automatically.\nultraOriginalVillain\nultraOriginalVillain\n\n4 years, 10 months ago\nalso elasticity implies scaling DOWN, automatically as well, in a timely manner.\nEGEmon\nEGEmon\n\n2 days, 11 hours ago\nSelected Answer:\nC\nasticity is the key benefit here.\nElasticity allows you to automatically scale your Azure resources (like the number of instances\nrunning your App1 application) up or down based on demand.\nChiquitabandita\nChiquitabandita\n\n1 month, 2 weeks ago\nCommunity vote distribution\nC (95%)\nD (5%)\n\nChiquitabandita\nChiquitabandita\n\n1 month, 2 weeks ago\nSelected Answer:\nC\nbased on comments here\nbigfooot15\nbigfooot15\n\n6 months, 2 weeks ago\nElastic computing is the ability to quickly expand or decrease computer processing, memory, and storage resources to meet\nchanging demands without worrying about capacity planning and engineering for peak usage.\nhttps://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/resources/cloud-computing-dictionary/what-is-elastic-\ncomputing#:~:text=Elastic%20computing%20is%20the%20ability,and%20engineering%20for%20peak%20usage.\nPigletTheProgrammer\nPigletTheProgrammer\n\n7 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nC\nC is right\nProdyna\nProdyna\n\n8 months ago\non exam 24.06.2024\nanswer: C\npoints: 952\nSR1234\nSR1234\n\n1 year, 3 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nC\ncorrect answer C\nKarmik\nKarmik\n\n1 year, 5 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nC\nC is right\nGoodman_5\nGoodman_5\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nC is correct.Elasticity stretches based on nedd\nrasbon\nrasbon\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\non 07/12/2023\nogmandalorian\nogmandalorian\n\n1 year, 10 months ago\nThe answer is C. elasticity. Azure Cloud Services can automatically adjust the resources allocated to the applicati",
