    "topic": 1,
    "type": "single",
    "question": "You have 1,000 virtual machines hosted on the Hyper-V hosts in a data center.\nYou plan to migrate all the virtual machines to an Azure pay-as-you-go subscription.\nYou need to identify which expenditure model to use for the planned Azure solution.\nWhich expenditure model should you identify?",
    "options": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "operational",
        "textZh": "營運的"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "elastic",
        "textZh": "彈性的"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "capital",
        "textZh": "資本"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "scalable",
        "textZh": "可擴充"
      }
    ],
    "answer": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answerText": "A",
    "comments": "rgalfaro\nrgalfaro\n\n5 years, 2 months ago\nThe expenditure models are either CapEx or OpEx (Capital or Operational). CapEx is what you pay upfront, on prem, for servers,\nracks, cooling, security, the Datacenter itself. OpEx is what you pay to keep your infrastructure operational, like IT staff. In this\ncase, when you move to the Cloud, what you identify in this case is the OpEx or Operational model. This is because you actually\ndon't have CapEx on the Cloud (or at least you look to minimize CapEx) as you pay for the resources you use and not for the\nunderlying hardware, security, cooling, etc that you will pay for in an On-Prem solution. That is why the right answer is (A)\nOperational. Elastic and Scalable are not expenditure models.\netyyr\netyyr\n\n5 years, 2 months ago\nThank you!\nStevIORI\nStevIORI\n\n4 years, 11 months ago\nThank you for the great inputs!\nAlison\nAlison\n\n4 years, 11 months ago\nCommunity vote distribution\nA (100%)\n\nGreat!\nGarry58\nGarry58\n\n4 years, 9 months ago\nwell said !!!!@ rgalfaro\nromansh\nromansh\n\n7 months, 1 week ago\nwell said\nAlonsochaves\nAlonsochaves\n\n11 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nOperational is Azure model\nintentando\nintentando\n\n1 year, 3 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cloud-adoption-framework/strategy/business-outcomes/fiscal-outcomes\nwsjones\nwsjones\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nThis showed up today. Had 36 questions and scored an 857, and the community and questions here were all covered on the test!\nardark\nardark\n\n1 year, 8 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nBurungunsatudy\nboy\nbuiducvu\nbuiducvu\n\n2 years, 2 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\npay-as-you-go = OpEx\nAlbertKwan\nAlbertKwan\n\n2 years, 3 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nOpEx :- is what you pay to keep your infrastructure operational, like IT staff.\nA is Correct Answer\nfin",
