    "comments": "chrisc10196\nchrisc10196\n\n2 years, 11 months ago\nI assume that when they say 'deploy', they mean actually racking a server yourself. You don't do this with Azure dedicated hosts\nso the answer is A.\nmaltezie\nmaltezie\n\n2 years, 8 months ago\nWell, it says \"physical servers\", so this should be easy points in the exam\nDeyvessh\nDeyvessh\n\n2 years, 8 months ago\nI think your are right, Its means you actually building a server yourself\nMIU\nMIU\n\n2 years, 9 months ago\nI think this is not only about Azure, just a general question.\nLaksiri\nLaksiri\n\n2 years, 11 months ago\nWe deploy only in private data centers. It comes under private cloud model and hybrid cloud models. So, the correct answer is A\n\n2 days, 11 hours ago\nCommunity vote distribution\nA (100%)\n\nEGEmon\nEGEmon\n\n2 days, 11 hours ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nPrivate and Hybrid Cloud\nzimzimzimma\nzimzimzimma\n\n7 months, 3 weeks ago\nGiven answer is correct, but:\n\"A private cloud is on-premises so you can deploy physical servers.\"\nNOT true - a private cloud doesn't have to mean on-premise. It can mean owned by a single organization.\nstaretheglaze\nstaretheglaze\n\n10 months, 3 weeks ago\npublic cloud is offered by Azure its there cloud so you can not deploy your server there. Hence private and hybrid.\nKanders\nKanders\n\n1 year ago\nA. private and hybrid cloud only\nbuiducvu\nbuiducvu\n\n1 year, 2 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nA. private cloud and hybrid cloud only\nPetersAzureAccount\nPetersAzureAccount\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nif you get this wrong you shouldn't be taking the test...\nminigold\nminigold\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nI am wondering, [ Private CLOUD = on-premise ] ?\nPrivate cloud is one of the cloud services,\nso how Private CLOUD can be equal on-premise?\nI heard that CLOUD is OFF-premise (opposite on-premise)\nJust let me know.\nAlbertKwan\nAlbertKwan",
