    "comments": "CK9797\nCK9797\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nHybrid\nkkJJc\nkkJJc\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\n\nkeywords: \"web-app\" and \"on-premises SQL Database\"\ntrashbox\ntrashbox\n\n3 weeks, 6 days ago\nHybrid: Azure (Public) + On prem\nYbra\nYbra\n\n1 month ago\nIf an Azure Web App can be hosted in a private cloud (on-premise in this case), that would be an example of Private\nCloud...right? So, the answer is not always an hybrid cloud...isn't it?\nSuper63\nSuper63\n\n4 months ago\nThe question betrays the answers. We have an AZURE WEB APP (on the cloud) that queries a\nlocal ON-PREMISES MS SQL Server\n(on-premise)\nThis is a clear case scenario of an hybrid cloud setup\nJawwad\nJawwad\n\n5 months, 1 week ago\nHybrid\nvedraj_1000\nvedraj_1000\n\n9 months ago\nhybrid\nsiculoct\nsiculoct\n\n9 months, 2 weeks ago\nhybrid\nemptyH\nemptyH\n\n2 years ago\nA little bit of on prem and a little bit of cloud = hybrid.\nhmax56\nhmax56\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nCorrecto\ngoncwil\ngoncwil\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nIs Hybrid, \"An Azure Web App (Public) x \"An MS SQL Server (Private)\"\nphuctran\nphuctran\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nWhy not Private?\nNCLatWorld\nNCLatWorld\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nAzure web app should be public cloud, and on-premises should be private cloud. Therefore, the answer is hybrid cloud.\nranjugowda\nranjugowda\n\n6 months, 2 weeks ago\nCool explaination..\nConviction454\nConviction454\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nI originally thought private as well, but I'm guessing because Azure Web would generally be categorized as a Public Cloud\nService, and On-prem is private... therefore hybrid. Sorry I don't have a better explanation.\n\nService, and On-prem is private... therefore hybrid. Sorry I don't have a better explanation.\nnmbuff\nnmbuff\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nwebsite host in cloud, database in on-premiss, therefore hybrid. i think!",
