    "comments": "Gepro\nGepro\n\n1 year, 5 months ago\nAzure Files is correct\nshivarama\nshivarama\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nIs other types asyn to azure?\nZoom2022\nZoom2022\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-firewall-and-proxy\nSuper63\nSuper63\n\n4 months ago\n\nSuper63\nSuper63\n\n4 months ago\nAzure Files offers fully managed file shares in the cloud that are accessible via\n* the industry standard Server Message Block (SMB) protocol\n* Network File System (NFS) protocol\n* and Azure Files REST API.\nAzure file shares can be mounted concurrently by cloud or on-premises deployments\nErasable_Mak\nErasable_Mak\n\n6 months, 2 weeks ago\nCpilot: The correct answer is Azure Files. Azure Files allows you to create file shares in the cloud that can be accessed via the\nSMB protocol, and it supports synchronization with on-premises storage using Azure File Sync.\nVaibhavGawali\nVaibhavGawali\n\n8 months, 1 week ago\nAzure Files is correct.\nAzure Files supports synchronization between on-premises storage and Azure Storage using Azure File Sync. This allows you to\ncentralize your file shares in Azure Files while keeping the flexibility, performance, and compatibility of an on-premises file\nserver.\nYomzie\nYomzie\n\n11 months, 1 week ago\nAzure File Sync is the name of the service that handles this.\npompali42\npompali42\n\n1 year ago\nits Files right?\nThanks millet",
