    "type": "hotspot",
    "question": "HOTSPOT -\nYou plan to extend your company's network to Azure.\nThe network contains a VPN appliance that uses an IP address of 131.107.200.1.\nYou need to create an Azure resource that defines the VPN appliance in Azure.\nWhich Azure resource should you create? To answer, select the appropriate resource in the answer area.\nHot Area:",
    "options": [],
    "answer": [],
    "answerText": "A Local Network Gateway is an object in Azure that represents your on-premise VPN device. A Virtual Network Gateway is\nthe VPN object at the Azure end of the\nVPN.\nA 'connection' is what connects the Local Network Gateway and the Virtual Network Gateway to bring up the VPN.\nThe local network gateway typically refers to your on-premises location. You give the site a name by which Azure can refer to\nit, then specify the IP address of the on-premises VPN device to which you will create a connection. You also specify the IP\naddress prefixes that will be routed through the VPN gateway to the VPN device. The address prefixes you specify are the\nprefixes located on your on-premises network. If your on-premises network changes or you need to change the public IP\naddress for the VPN device, you can easily update the values later.\nReference:\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/vpn-gateway-howto-site-to-site-resource-manager-portal",
    "comments": "BL101\nBL101\n\n3 years, 4 months ago\nI didn't get this at first - but then re-read the question - the clue is in the extension to Azure which indicates you are on Prem -\nso you need a Local Network Gateway - that's why people who said Virtual Network Gateway are wrong\n2ffc8ff\n2ffc8ff\n\n2 months ago\nIndeed! This is tricky question and the answer is of course in the question itself. This may help explain better:\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/tutorial-site-to-site-portal\nFoow\nFoow\n\n3 years, 1 month ago\nIs the word \"appliance\" also not a flag for recognizing that it is on-premise?\nRougePotatoe\nRougePotatoe\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nIn support of this answer. Read what is local network gateway. The local network gateway is a specific object that represents\nyour on-premises location (the site) for routing purposes. You give the site a name by which Azure can refer to it, then specify\nthe IP address of the on-premises VPN device to which you'll create a connection. You also specify the IP address prefixes\nthat will be routed through the VPN gateway to the VPN device. The address prefixes you specify are the prefixes located on\nyour on-premises network. If your on-premises network changes or you need to change the public IP address for the VPN\ndevice, you can easily update the values later.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/tutorial-site-to-site-portal\nVinnyMacD\nVinnyMacD\n\n1 year, 6 months ago\nLocal - means creating a resource in your DC.\nAsk is - You need to create an \"Azure resource\" that defines the VPN \"appliance in Azure.\"\nAnswer is - Virtual Network Gateway.\nrekab18\nrekab18\n\n1 year, 1 month ago\nThe Virtual Network Gateway in Azure is used to create a VPN connection between your on-premises network and Azure. It\n\nThe Virtual Network Gateway",
    "references": [
      "https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/vpn-gateway-howto-site-to-site-resource-manager-portal",
      "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/tutorial-site-to-site-",
      "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/tutorial-site-to-site-portal",
      "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/vpn-gateway-about-vpn-devices",
      "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/enterprise/connect-an-on-premises-network-to-a-microsoft-azure-virtual-"
    ],
    "questionZh": "熱點 -\n您計劃將公司的網路擴展到 Azure。\n此網路包含使用 IP 位址 131.107.200.1 的 VPN 裝置。\n您需要建立一個在 Azure 中定義 VPN 裝置的 Azure 資源。\n您應該建立哪種 Azure 資源？要回答，請在答案區域中選擇適當的資源。\n熱門區域：",
    "answerTextZh": "本機網路閘道是 Azure 中的一個對象，代表本機 VPN 設備。虛擬網路網關是\nAzure 端的 VPN 對象\nVPN。\n「連線」是連接本機閘道和虛擬閘道以啟動 VPN 的連線。\n本地網路網關通常是指您的本地位置。您為網站指定名稱，Azure 可以透過該名稱來引用該網站\n它，然後指定您要建立連接的本機 VPN 裝置的 IP 位址。您也指定IP\n將透過 VPN 閘道路由到 VPN 設備的位址前綴。您指定的地址前綴是\n位於本地網路上的前綴。如果您的本機網路發生變化或您需要變更公用IP\nVPN 裝置的位址，您可以稍後輕鬆更新這些值。\n參考：\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/vpn-gateway-howto-site-to-site-resource-manager-portal"
