    "answerText": "Correct Answer:\n\nBox 1: Yes -\nYou can use the same account to manage multiple subscriptions.\nYou can create an additional subscription for your account\nin the Azure portal. You may want an additional subscription to avoid hitting subscription limits, to create separate\nenvironments for security, or to isolate data for compliance reasons.\nBox 2: No -\nYou cannot merge two subscriptions into a single subscription.\nHowever, you can move some Azure resources from one\nsubscription to another.\nYou can also transfer ownership of a subscription and change the billing type for a subscription.\nBox 3: Yes -\nA company can have multiple subscriptions and store resources in the different subscriptions.\nHowever, a resource instance\ncan exist in only one subscription.\nReference:\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/manage/create-subscription",
    "comments": "puj\npuj\n\n3 years, 5 months ago\nCorrect\nkenluong\nkenluong\n\n3 years, 1 month ago\nwhat you mean correct ?\nGresch123123\nGresch123123\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nit is chosen\norlandoryo\norlandoryo\n\n1 year, 6 months ago\nMeaning agreement with the answer given.\nzimzimzimma\nzimzimzimma\n\n1 year, 2 months ago\ncorrect!\ndkaps06\ndkaps06\n\n1 year ago\ncorrect\nJW023\nJW023\n\n10 months, 2 weeks ago\nCorrect, i have spoken.\nAxz\nAxz\n\n2 years, 6 months ago\nCorrect\n\nCorrect\npigandarias\npigandarias\n\n3 years, 4 months ago\nAppeared in 05/04/21 exam\nsiculoct\nsiculoct\n\n3 months, 1 week ago\ncorrect . Yes, No, Yes\nAGTraining\nAGTraining\n\n4 months, 4 weeks ago\nCorrect\nJuanpnav\nJuanpnav\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nCorrect, but you can merge subscriptions by contacting support and they may make an exception. But you can't merge\nsubscriptions by default so Y/N/Y is correct.\nunVatoLoco\nunVatoLoco\n\n1 year, 6 months ago\nWas on exam 03/02/23\nahashemi\nahashemi\n\n1 year, 8 months ago\nAppeared on Dec 9 2022 exam\nurbanbushman\nurbanbushman\n\n1 year, 9 months ago\nCorrect\nLazylinux\nLazylinux\n\n2 years ago\ncorrect is YNY\nemp207\nemp207\n\n2 years ago\nBy the way we can merge subbsciptions by creating a ticket with microsoft\nKhlinton\nKhlinton\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nAnswer is No, No, Yes.\nYou cannot create an azure subscription with a Microsoft account.\nCHRIS12722222\nCHRIS12722222\n\n2 years ago\nThis is not correct. See link below\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/guides/developer/azure-developer-\nguide#:~:text=To%20create%20or,by%20Azure%20AD\nPa1theAchiever\nPa1theAchiever\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nYes No Yes\nAmyPain\nAmyPain\n\n2 years, 2 months ago\nA little misleading. See question 60.\n\nA little misleading. See question 60.\nYou can't use a Microsoft account, you need an AAD account to manage a subscription.\nsamraw83\nsamraw83\n\n2 years, 1 mon",
