    "comments": "7v\n7v\n\n4 years, 6 months ago\nWindows 10 run SMB so File service in Storage account is a better answer.\nHHHo\nHHHo\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nGot this in exam on 2022.04.18\nsaim18\nsaim18\n\n8 months, 1 week ago\nMicrosoft test are much easier than these\nnanny123\nnanny123\n\n6 months, 1 week ago\nIs it?\nSAFM\nSAFM\n\n11 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nC\nCommunity vote distribution\nC (100%)\n\nAzure File Storage\njana90\njana90\n\n1 year, 1 month ago\nAzure Files shares can be mounted concurrently by cloud or on-premises deployments of Windows, Linux, and macOS. Azure\nFiles shares can also be cached on Windows Servers with Azure File Sync for fast access near where the data is being used.\nsemauni\nsemauni\n\n1 year, 3 months ago\nCan anyone tell me why you would exclude D, blob storage? I would think that any kind of file could be stored on a drive.\nAZFabio\nAZFabio\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nC\n\"Mapping a network drive\" points to file share.\nunVatoLoco\nunVatoLoco\n\n1 year, 6 months ago\nWas on exam 03/02/23\nBereket\nBereket\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nIt’s C\nTo create a storage solution in Azure for mapping a network drive from computers running Windows 10, you will need to create an\nAzure file share.\nAn Azure file share is a managed file storage service that enables you to create a shared network drive in Azure\nand access it from any device that supports the SMB (Server Message Block) protocol, including computers running Windows 10.\nLuansi\nLuansi\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nC\nTo create a storage solution in Azure for mapping a network drive from computers running Windows 10, you will need to create an\nAzure file share.\nAn Azure file share is a managed file storage service that enables you to create a shared network drive in Azure and access it\nfrom any device that supports the SMB (Serv",
    "references": [],
    "questionZh": "你打算將網路磁碟機從執行 Windows 10 的多台電腦對應到 Azure 儲存體。\n您需要在 Azure 中為規劃的對應磁碟機建立儲存解決方案。\n你該創造什麼？",
    "answerTextZh": "C"
