    "comments": "SiDoCiOuS\nSiDoCiOuS\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nWas on exam 11/03/2022. Answer is good!\ntacobear\ntacobear\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nit was on exam on 03/12/2022.\nYuraq\nYuraq\n\n9 months, 2 weeks ago\n\nAn Availability Zone is a physically separate zone, within an Azure region.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/availability\nDtex69\nDtex69\n\n1 year, 5 months ago\nI think this is wrong - a region has up to three availability zones, each availability zone is in a datacentre. The question asks\nabout an availability zone - i.e. singular - so it should be datacenter not region.\nSAFM\nSAFM\n\n11 months ago\nActually, each availability zone can have three datacenters inside it, so the AZ is a container of datacenters.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/availability-zones-overview?tabs=azure-cli\nSAFM\nSAFM\n\n11 months ago\nmultiple datacenters (not only three) can be inside one availability zone. Three AZs can be inside one region.\nvishnut1986\nvishnut1986\n\n5 months, 2 weeks ago\nNo, you are wrong because availability zone itself consists of one of more Data centers, so B is correct.\nJC_de_Sevilla\nJC_de_Sevilla\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nCorrecto\nPa1theAchiever\nPa1theAchiever\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\ncorrect\nDiallo18\nDiallo18\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nWas on exam 03/03/2022\n[Removed]\n[Removed]\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nWas on exam 26/02/2022\nMS_Learner\nMS_Learner\n\n2 years, 6 months ago\nGot Feb 10, 2022\ngarmatey\ngarmatey\n\n2 years, 7 months ago\nThe question says Availability Zones HAVE\nlocations but then the answer says Availability Zones ARE locations...\nABarrios\nABarrios\n\n2 years, 7 months ago\nI passed the exam today: 20/01/2022 I got this question\nakp1000\nakp1000\n\n2 years, 7 months ago\nIf you don't know the answer to this go back and study\nPapagaio\nPapagaio\n\n1 year, 7 months a",
