    "comments": "vansardo\nvansardo\n\n11 months, 3 weeks ago\nThird is NO. You can configure UDRs between two subnets in different virtual networks.\nWazery\nWazery\n\n1 week, 1 day ago\n\"Network security groups (NSGs) can contain multiple inbound and outbound security rules.\"\n- Ja – NSGs können mehrere eingehende und ausgehende Sicherheitsregeln enthalten.\n\"A VM that performs a particular function such as running a firewall is also called a Network virtual appliance.\"\n- Ja – Eine virtuelle Maschine, die eine spezielle Funktion ausführt (z. B. eine Firewall), wird als Network Virtual Appliance (NVA)\nbezeichnet.\n\"A user-defined route (UDR) can only control network traffic between subnets of a single virtual network.\"\n- Nein – UDRs können den Datenverkehr nicht nur innerhalb eines einzelnen virtuellen Netzwerks steuern, sondern auch den\nVerkehr zu On-Premises-Netzwerken oder anderen VNETs über Peering.\n\nVerkehr zu On-Premises-Netzwerken oder anderen VNETs über Peering.\njambroba\njambroba\n\n7 months ago\n- suggested answer is correct, it's Y,Y,N.\nPouwen\nPouwen\n\n8 months ago\nIs Y,Y,N\nThe statement \"A user-defined route (UDR) can only control network traffic between subnets of a single virtual network\" is\nincorrect.\nIn Azure, user-defined routes (UDRs) can indeed control network traffic within a single virtual network, but they can also\ninfluence traffic to destinations outside of the virtual network. This includes routing traffic to on-premises networks through\nVPN gateways, peered virtual networks, or even the internet via a Network Virtual Appliance (NVA).\nPouwen\nPouwen\n\n8 months ago\nIs Y,Y,N\njeevanss\njeevanss\n\n10 months, 4 weeks ago\n3 - keyword is only - so its No\nA User Defined Route (UDR) in Azure can control network traffic not only within a single Virtual Network (VNet) but also\nbetween differe",
