    "comments": "wmlead\nwmlead\n\n3 years, 8 months ago\nthe answer is A and D\ninkyz\ninkyz\n\n2 years, 10 months ago\nWas on exam 24/03/2022 - Answer is Correct (A & D)\nSAFM\nSAFM\n\n1 year, 5 months ago\nSo, it was possible to select more than one answer?\nasduta\nasduta\n\n5 months, 3 weeks ago\nyes as the question asked for 2 answers\nwsjones\nwsjones\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nShowed up today. Great question bank, and passed with an 857. Thanks to all!\nCommunity vote distribution\nAD (89%)\nA (11%)\n\nShowed up today. Great question bank, and passed with an 857. Thanks to all!\ndgerok\ndgerok\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nAD\nAD are the right choices\nFutureAdmin\nFutureAdmin\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nThis was on exam. 9/30/23\nSAFM\nSAFM\n\n1 year, 5 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nThe key is the \"single datacenter\" which indicates the proposal of the AZs = same region. If the requirement were to protect\nagainst \"regional failure\" then it should be D.\nSavik\nSavik\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nQuestion on 07/07/2023 exam\nAZFabio\nAZFabio\n\n1 year, 10 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nAD\ncorrect\nAlgates\nAlgates\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\ncame in exam today\nidreessal\nidreessal\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nBro,\nhow many question did you expected from the exam topic\nbuiducvu\nbuiducvu\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nSelected Answer:\nAD\nthe answer is A and D\nDan1223\nDan1223\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nA and D\nPa1theAchiever\nPa1theAchiever\n\n2 years, 7 months ago\nA and D\ngabrisiq\ngabrisiq\n\n2 years, 8 months ago\nDeploying VM's in two or more Regions is the same as deploying in two or more Availability Zones. A & D.\n[Removed]\n[Removed]\n\n2 years ago\nThis is not correct. There can be multiple Availability Zones in one Region.\nAlthough, they're both providing a solution for the stated problem.\n\nAlthough, they're both providing a solution for the stated problem.\ncuentaa",
