    "comments": "vanr2000\nvanr2000\n\n5 years, 6 months ago\nThis is totally valid. Run the script from a computer that runs Chrome OS and uses Azure Cloud Shell to run Powershell scripts fo\nrazure. Why doesn't meet the needs?\nNebula09\nNebula09\n\n4 years, 5 months ago\nYou are correct given answer is incorrect. Answer is YES.\nReddybo\nReddybo\n\n4 years, 2 months ago\nThe PS script should be already uploaded to the Azure Storage to be able to run it from the Cloud Shell.. Is it already uploaded?\nWe don't know that.. It's only says to run the script from the computer, and not from the Azure portal..\njoondez\njoondez\n\n4 years, 5 months ago\nCommunity vote distribution\nA (100%)\n\nMany people think this is a trick question because you cannot install CLI onto Chrome OS. However, I think this question is way\nmore straightforward. You can use Cloud Shell in the Chrome browser. This works on all OS. This question is being used to\ndemonstrate that the Cloud Shell can run on all OS.\nTolulee\nTolulee\n\n4 years, 9 months ago\nBecause you can't install Powershell on Chrom OS, the Mac question gives this away\nFcnet\nFcnet\n\n4 years, 9 months ago\nthat's wrong with azure cli you can and from cloud shell you can run a script too\nConaxLearn\nConaxLearn\n\n4 years, 6 months ago\nNo need to install PowerShell when running PowerShell script in Cloud Shell.\nMartinMystere\nMartinMystere\n\n5 years, 1 month ago\nI have read all the comments and I believe everybody missed the point. The question states Chrome OS and not Chrome Web\nBrowser.\nhttps://www.google.com/chromebook/chrome-os/\nErasable_Mak\nErasable_Mak\n\n6 months, 2 weeks ago\nChrome OS comes with the Chrome browser built-in. so yes\npurav1009\npurav1009\n\n5 years, 1 month ago\nYep. There's no mention of any web browser.\nlejozapata\nlejozapata\n\n5 years ago\nBut is a complicated question",
