    "comments": "Su_L\nSu_L\n\n4 years ago\nthe image is cut-off at bottom, at the end on this Menu list you will see 'Help + Support' listed as a Menu option that's the\ncorrect answer\nzimzimzimma\nzimzimzimma\n\n1 year, 8 months ago\nDon't think the image is cut off, if you choose 'Dashboard' you will be presented with a 'Service Health' option in the\ndashboard. I see it in my subscription and I didn't put it there. It's there by default next to 'Marketplace'.\nCorrect answer should be Dashboard.\nkoian\nkoian\n\n3 years, 11 months ago\nHome > Help + support > Service Health > Planned maintenance\njambroba\njambroba\n\n6 months, 4 weeks ago\nDashboard\n\nNoursBear\nNoursBear\n\n7 months ago\nToday 22.7-24.\nIf I go to Azure Portal, I can go to Dashboard, there I have a button \"Service Health\" OR I can go to help and\nsupport, then I have Service Health. Don't forget many of the comments are many years ago.\nMaggieXLin\nMaggieXLin\n\n8 months, 1 week ago\nI checked in the azure portal there are 2 ways to access service health. 1st) dashboard scroll to the bottom > service health 2nd)\nHelp + support > under support Service health\nMaggieXLin\nMaggieXLin\n\n8 months, 1 week ago\nI did notice when you go the first way it doesn't show planned maintenance therefore the answer would be 2nd way.\nYomzie\nYomzie\n\n11 months, 2 weeks ago\nI wish it were possible to crop and paste \"screenshot\" images in here, so as to avoid all these confusion and assumptions...\nFrom the Azure Portal Home >> Dashboard >> Service Health (right there at the bottom left corner of the Dashboard page).\nThere should be no more argument about this, please!!\nJmumbua\nJmumbua\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nDashboard>Help+Support> Service Health\nMAHA1004\nMAHA1004\n\n1 year, 5 months ago\nDashboard >Help+Support| Service health> Planned Maintenance\nVinnyMacD\nVinnyMacD\n\n1 year,",
