    "answerTextZh": "Box 1: Overview -\nWhen you assign roles, you must specify a scope. Scope is the set of resources the access applies to. In Azure, you can\nspecify a scope at four levels from broad to narrow: 管理群組, 訂用帳戶, 資源群組, and resource.\n1. Sign in to the Azure portal.\n2. In the Search box at the top, search for the scope you want to grant access to. For example, search for Management\ngroups, 訂用帳戶s, 資源群組s, or a specific resource.\n3. Click the specific resource for that scope.\n4. The following shows an example 資源群組.\n\nBox 2: Access control (IAM)\nAccess control (IAM) is the page that you typically use to assign roles to grant access to Azure resources. It's also known as\nidentity and access management\n(IAM) and appears in several locations in the Azure portal.\n1. Click Access control (IAM).\nThe following shows an example of the Access control (IAM) page for a 資源群組.\n2. Click the Role assignments tab to view the role assignments at this scope.\n3. Click Add > Add role assignment.\nIf you don't have permissions to assign roles, the Add role assignment option will be disabled.\n4. The Add role assignment page opens.\n參考資料:\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/role-assignments-portal"
