    "question": "Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a\nunique solution that might meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others\nmight not have a correct solution.\nAfter you answer a question in this section, you will NOT be able to return to it. As a result, these questions will not appear in\nthe review screen.\nYour Azure environment contains multiple Azure virtual machines.\nYou need to ensure that a virtual machine named VM1 is accessible from the Internet over HTTP.\nSolution: You modify an Azure Traffic Manager profile.\nDoes this meet the goal?",
    "options": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "Yes",
        "textZh": "是的"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "No",
        "textZh": "否"
      }
    ],
    "answer": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answerText": "B\nAzure Traffic Manager is a DNS-based load balancing solution.\nIt is not used to ensure that a virtual machine named VM1 is\naccessible from the Internet over\nHTTP.\nTo ensure that a virtual machine named VM1 is accessible from the Internet over HTTP, you need to modify a network\nsecurity group or Azure Firewall.\nIn this question, we need to add a rule to a network security group or Azure Firewall to allow the connection to the virtual\nmachine on port 80 (HTTP).\nReferences:\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-overview",
    "comments": "pcce5w2hlh\npcce5w2hlh\n\n5 years, 1 month ago\nAnswer is B.\nBecoz Traffic Manager is used to distribute traffic at DNS level across different regions.\nCommunity vote distribution\nB (100%)\n\nClouddog\nClouddog\n\n4 years, 7 months ago\nhttps://azure.microsoft.com/nl-nl/resources/videos/how-azure-traffic-manager-works/\ngassen\ngassen\n\n4 years, 8 months ago\njust for the future\nIf the Question doesn't raise any question please stop posting comments, it's a source of frustration and Confusion\nnick1970\nnick1970\n\n4 years, 6 months ago\n100 thumbs up. So true.\nEnits\nEnits\n\n4 years, 2 months ago\nIts good to get broader perspective from different people\nMickeyG\nMickeyG\n\n4 years, 6 months ago\nI agree, but only when users just respond with \"correct\" or \"A is correct\". This adds nothing for the rest of us. I enjoy having\ncontext why options are invalid or valid. But responding with just the letter that is the answer is not helpful to anyone\nmr_corte\nmr_corte\n\n3 years, 7 months ago\n\"correct\"\nPiiri565\nPiiri565\n\n4 years, 6 months ago\nI think comments make the concepts to understand much better, just by knowing the answer and moving to the next question.Let\nthe people connect .Its the source of Knowledge\nNathan12345\nNathan12345\n\n6 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nB\ntraffic manager like LB\nChristian_garcia_martin\nChristian_garcia_martin\n\n7 months, 2 weeks ago\nyou can do that with NGS so answer is not\nChristian_garcia_martin\nChristian_garcia_martin\n\n7 months, 3 weeks ago\nwhen you create a VM you need to set the NSG to allow traffic under HTTP protocol (for example) in a specific port.\nb274b54\nb274b54\n\n8 months, 2 weeks ago\nI cannot find the service \"Traffic Manager\" in the most recent AZ-900 study guide, I guess we can skip this question\ncristianosilva\ncristianosilva\n\n1 year, 6 months ago\nAnswer is B\nI",
    "references": [
      "https://azure.microsoft.com/nl-nl/resources/videos/how-azure-traffic-manager-works/",
      "https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-overview",
      "https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/network-security-groups-overview",
      "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/guide/technology-choices/load-balancing-overview#decision-tree-for-load-"
    ],
    "questionZh": "注意：此題屬於一系列使用相同案例的題組。每題會提供一個可能符合目標的獨特解決方案；有些題組可能有多個正確解，有些則可能沒有正確解。\n在此區段作答後將無法返回上一題，因此這些題目不會出現在複查畫面中。\n你的 Azure 環境包含多部 Azure 虛擬機器。\n你需要確保名為 VM1 的虛擬機器可透過 HTTP 從網際網路存取。\n解決方案： 你修改 an Azure Traffic Manager profile.\n這是否符合目標？",
    "answerTextZh": "B\nAzure Traffic Manager is a DNS-based load balancing solution.\nIt is not used to ensure that a 虛擬機器 named VM1 is\naccessible from the Internet over\nHTTP.\nTo ensure that a 虛擬機器 named VM1 is accessible from the Internet over HTTP, you need to modify a network\nsecurity group or Azure Firewall.\nIn this question, we need to add a rule to a 網路安全性群組 or Azure Firewall to allow the connection to the virtual\nmachine on port 80 (HTTP).\n參考資料:\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-overview"
