    "comments": "sheddy\nsheddy\n\n4 years ago\nKeyword is \"several\". You will want to use a group for multiple VMs traffic rules.\nRainman\nRainman\n\n3 years, 8 months ago\nbut i was expecting to see either \"A fire wall\" or \"multiple NSGs\" .\nLexusNX425\nLexusNX425\n\n3 years, 6 months ago\nYou could have multiple VMs in a single NSG\nsuccess101\nsuccess101\n\n4 years, 1 month ago\nA is correct\nshashu07\nshashu07\n\n3 years, 3 months ago\nKeyword is \"web servers and several database servers to Azure\" ie internal traffic to VMs, so answer is NSG.\nCommunity vote distribution\nA (100%)\n\nKeyword is \"web servers and several database servers to Azure\" ie internal traffic to VMs, so answer is NSG.\nWe can consider Firewall, its point to external traffic to VMs\nkaushu400\nkaushu400\n\n4 years ago\noh really?\nnexter\nnexter\n\n4 years ago\noh yeah\ngetazusername\ngetazusername\n\n3 years, 3 months ago\nouh yeah!\nElPile\nElPile\n\n5 months, 1 week ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nA. network security groups (NSGs)\nLS1030\nLS1030\n\n11 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nNetwork Security Group has the functionality to allow and/or deny access to an azure resource.\nAzureCloud07\nAzureCloud07\n\n1 year, 2 months ago\nNetwork Security Group (NSG) is like\ninternal firewall inside your Virtual Network\nright before your resources\n- A (right answer)\nTonyghostR05\nTonyghostR05\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nNSG, other choice is not work\nLeito82\nLeito82\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nKey word is \"limit\".\nA NSG does just that.\nKrissy90\nKrissy90\n\n1 year, 11 months ago\nNSG Must be something like NetworkPolices for Kubernetes.\nfercho\nfercho\n\n2 years, 5 months ago\nAppeared on 05 Sep 2021\ntaoj\ntaoj\n\n2 years, 8 months ago\nGot it on 01 Jun 2021\nGerardo1971\nGerardo1971\n\n2 years, 9 months ago\nCorrect answer\nSiwe\nSiwe\n\n2 years, 9 months ago\nDefinately NSG\n\nDefinately NSG\nshalinics1211111\nshalinics",
