    "comments": "Ragijo\nRagijo\n\n4 years, 9 months ago\nNSG just block or open a port, Azure Firewall can \"limit the amount of traffic\", because it's a stateful firewall. So the answer is\nAzure Firewall (\nExaminicus\nExaminicus\n\n4 years, 5 months ago\nBoth NSG and Firewall can perform this function. I believe the key is in the number of virtual networks involved. You will use an\nNSG for a single VN and a Firewall for multiple.\nKashan_Ali\nKashan_Ali\n\n4 years, 1 month ago\nExactly, when I read that I need to protect them all then I have selected \"Azure Firewall\".\nultraOriginalVillain\nultraOriginalVillain\n\n4 years, 4 months ago\nYes! NSGs need to be created 10 times for all 10 VNets. Firewall can be applied to a resource group, etc. etc. AT ONCE,\nselecting all of them together. Imagine you had 1,000 VNets as well !\nCommunity vote distribution\nD (100%)\n\nJovial\nJovial\n\n4 years, 1 month ago\nYes , and another thing is the cost . the cost of peering between 10 Vnet is going to be huge compared to cost of Azure\nFirewall.\nsiculoct\nsiculoct\n\n2 months, 3 weeks ago\nD. Azure Firewall\nkaf_omic\nkaf_omic\n\n8 months, 1 week ago\nSelected Answer:\nD\nOne Azure Firewall for all vnets\nMANANDAVEY\nMANANDAVEY\n\n1 year, 1 month ago\nSelected Answer:\nD\nD is the correct answer.\nAtul_0902\nAtul_0902\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nQuestion is not about protect but You need to limit the amount of inbound traffic..\ndoubtful about Azure Firewall.\nzellck\nzellck\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nD\nD is the answer.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall/overview\nAzure Firewall is a cloud-native and intelligent network firewall security service that provides the best of breed threat\nprotection for your cloud workloads running in Azure. It's a fully stateful, firewall as a service with built-in high availability and\nunrestricted",
    "references": [
      "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall/overview"
    ],
