    "answerText": "Box 1: No -\nAzure Active Directory (Azure AD) is a cloud-based service.\nIt does not require domain controllers on virtual machines.\nBox 2: Yes -\nAzure Active Directory (Azure AD) is a centralized identity provider in the cloud. This is the primary built-in authentication\nand authorization service to provide secure access to Azure resources and Microsoft 365.\nBox 3: No -\nUser accounts in Azure Active Directory can be assigned multiple licenses for different Azure or Microsoft 365 services.",
    "comments": "panal\npanal\n\n3 years ago\nCorrect\ngabrisiq\ngabrisiq\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nalmost all questions that include \"...only\" are answered with \"No\"\nLofi_bansoa\nLofi_bansoa\n\n3 months ago\nThank you for your comment i havn't noticed until you said it\nwsjones\nwsjones\n\n4 months ago\nShowed up today.\nFutureAdmin\nFutureAdmin\n\n4 months, 3 weeks ago\nThis was on exam. 9/30/23\nzellck\nzellck\n\n1 year, 1 month ago\nNYN is the answer.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/active-directory/enterprise-users/licensing-groups-resolve-problems#more-than-one-\nproduct-license-assigned-to-a-group\nYou can assign more than one product license to a group. For example, you can assign Office 365 Enterprise E3 and Enterprise\nMobility + Security to a group to easily enable all included services for users.\nAzure AD attempts to assign all licenses that are specified in the group to each user. If Azure AD can't assign one of the\nproducts because of business logic problems, it won't assign the other licenses in the group either. An example is if there aren't\nenough licenses for all, or if there are conflicts with other services that are enabled on the user.\nYou can see the users who failed to get assigned and check which products are affected by this problem.\nkamal_004\nkamal_004\n\n1 year, 3 months ago\nAnswer: No Yes No\nraul4real73\nraul4real73\n\n1 year, 8 months ago\n2 is NO.\nAzure AD helps users access both external and internal resources.\n\nAzure AD helps users access both external and internal resources.\nExternal resources might include Microsoft Office 365, the Azure portal, and thousands of other software as a service (SaaS)\napplications.\nInternal resources might include apps on your corporate network and intranet, along with any cloud applications developed\nwithin your organization.\nkapy024\nkapy024\n\n1 year, 8",
    "references": [
      "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/active-directory/enterprise-users/licensing-groups-resolve-problems#more-than-one-"
    ],
    "questionZh": "熱點 -\n對於以下每個陳述，如果該陳述為真，請選擇「是」。否則，選擇否。\n注意：每個正確的選擇都值得一分。\n熱門區域：",
    "answerTextZh": "Box 1: 否 -\nAzure Active Directory (Azure AD) is a cloud-based service.\nIt does not require domain controllers on 虛擬機器s.\nBox 2: 是 -\nAzure Active Directory (Azure AD) is a centralized identity provider in the cloud. This is the primary built-in authentication\nand authorization service to provide secure access to Azure resources and Microsoft 365.\nBox 3: 否 -\nUser accounts in Azure Active Directory can be assigned multiple licenses for different Azure or Microsoft 365 services."
