    "comments": "El_Zammo\nEl_Zammo\n\n3 years, 3 months ago\nHow is this even a question? What policy?\nMozbius_\nMozbius_\n\n3 years, 2 months ago\nYup. Answer is obviously B based on keyword \"policy\" but the question on its own is straight garbage!\njoergsi\njoergsi\n\n3 years, 1 month ago\nMaybe we have this question in the next exam:\nWhat is the difference between Water?\nvinc855\nvinc855\n\n3 years, 4 months ago\nCorrect answer\nSuper63\nSuper63\n\n3 months, 4 weeks ago\nCommunity vote distribution\nB (100%)\n\nOften in\nMS exams we must eliminate the incorrect answers first:\nA- a read-only lock\n- locks resources from being modified/deleted\nC- Azure management groups provide a level of scope above subscriptions. You organize subscriptions into containers called\nmanagement groups and apply your governance conditions to the management groups.This manages SUBSCRIPTIONS\nD- Azure reservation: Azure Reserved Instances are an Azure pricing plan that can help you reduce cloud costs.\nSo in spite of a very badly formulated question the only plausible answer is: B- An Azure Policy\nShruti2024\nShruti2024\n\n6 months, 1 week ago\nThe wording is confusing. What is this asking?\nNoursBear\nNoursBear\n\n7 months ago\nQuestion is surely incomplete and worded differently by MS\nTehkl\nTehkl\n\n10 months, 1 week ago\nits in the exam - 17-April-2024\nArtC\nArtC\n\n1 year, 1 month ago\nGot this question on 12-10-23\n3d1d88d\n3d1d88d\n\n1 year, 1 month ago\nthis question is vague. How does a policy meet a policy requirement??\nzellck\nzellck\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nSelected Answer:\nB\nB is the answer.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview\nAzure Policy helps to enforce organizational standards and to assess compliance at-scale. Through its compliance dashboard, it\nprovides an aggregated view to evaluate the overall state of the en",
