    "answerText": "Authentication, not authorization is the process of verifying a user's credentials.\nThe difference between authentication and authorization is:\n- Authentication is proving your identity, proving that you are who you say you are. The most common example of this is\nlogging in to a system by providing credentials such as a username and password.\n- Authorization is what you're allowed to do once you've been authenticated. For example, what resources you're allowed to\naccess and what you can do with those resources.",
    "comments": "nickosems\nnickosems\n\n3 years, 9 months ago\nAnswer is correct. Authentication verifies and validates your credentials.\nAuthorization validates what resource you have access to.\n\nefb9f47\nefb9f47\n\n9 months, 2 weeks ago\nAuthentication = \"e\" like credentials.\nAuthorization = \"o\" like resource\njambroba\njambroba\n\n7 months ago\n- Authentication is correct\nblacksheep1\nblacksheep1\n\n1 year ago\nGot this 5 febr 2024\nPal0801\nPal0801\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nGot this 30 Sept 2023\nmsmt\nmsmt\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\non the exam on 29jun2023\nzellck\nzellck\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\n\"Authentication\" is the answer.\nMS_Learner\nMS_Learner\n\n3 years ago\nGot Feb 10, 2022, with a different definition. asking somethnig about establishing user identity to validate the resource you are\nasking to have access to..I picked authorization instead of Authentication.\nLB187\nLB187\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nyea i get why you selected authorization , sneaky \"to validate\" but initially it asks \"establishing user identity\"\nTarfa\nTarfa\n\n3 years, 2 months ago\nappear 16Dec21\nlovecloud2\nlovecloud2\n\n3 years, 2 months ago\nFree points I guess\nRichC\nRichC\n\n3 years, 2 months ago\nappear 26 Nov\nifysfriend\nifysfriend\n\n3 years, 9 months ago\nAnswer is correct.\nlollo1234\nlollo1234\n\n3 years, 9 months ago\nAsked during exam on 21 May 2021.\nkandascan\nkandascan\n\n3 years, 9 months ago\n\nCorrect answer\nhlacoucou\nhlacoucou\n\n3 years, 10 months ago\nI had this question in the exam 19/04/2021\n[Removed]\n[Removed]\n\n3 years, 10 months ago\ngot this q\nTas006\nTas006\n\n3 years, 11 months ago\nAnswer is correct",
    "references": [],
    "questionZh": "熱點 -\n要完成句子，請在答案區中選擇適當的選項。\n熱門區域：",
    "answerTextZh": "Authentication, not authorization is the process of verifying a user's credentials.\nThe difference between authentication and authorization is:\n- Authentication is proving your identity, proving that you are who you say you are. The most common example of this is\nlogging in to a system by providing credentials such as a username and password.\n- Authorization is what you're allowed to do once you've been authenticated. For example, what resources you're allowed to\naccess and what you can do with those resources."
