    "comments": "Nick74\nNick74\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nWas on test October 14 2022\nShadiAwwad\nShadiAwwad\n\n8 months, 1 week ago\nSelected Answer:\nD\nD is the answer.\ngilldilraj\ngilldilraj\n\n11 months ago\nTrust Center should be used to identify whether Azure complies with your company's regional requirements\nzellck\nzellck\n\n1 year, 1 month ago\nSelected Answer:\nD\nD is the answer.\nhttps://www.microsoft.com/en-sg/trust-center/product-overview\nCommunity vote distribution\nD (100%)\n\nzellck\nzellck\n\n1 year, 1 month ago\nThe Trust Center is a website that provides information about the security, privacy, and compliance of Azure services. It includes\ninformation about compliance certifications, standards, and regulations that Azure meets or that customers can use to assess\nAzure's compliance with their own requirements. It will give you the overview of what certifications Azure has achieved and the\ncompliance standards it meets. This can help you determine if Azure meets the company's regional requirements.\ndsem771\ndsem771\n\n1 year, 9 months ago\nCorrect\njoergsi\njoergsi\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nMicrosoft Trust Center:\nhttps://www.microsoft.com/en-ie/trust-center/privacy\nakp1000\nakp1000\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nSelected Answer:\nD\nCorrect\nLincoln01\nLincoln01\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nCorrect",
