    "comments": "t213\nt213\n\n2 years, 3 months ago\nExam question 08-05-2021\nRS66\nRS66\n\n3 months, 3 weeks ago\nRTO and RPO = uptime\nrafacop\nrafacop\n\n4 months, 1 week ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nI've choosen A by discard.\nfloradu88\nfloradu88\n\n5 months, 3 weeks ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nIt can only be A\nzellck\nzellck\n\n7 months, 2 weeks ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nCommunity vote distribution\nA (88%)\nB (12%)\n\nA is the answer.\nhttps://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/support/legal/sla/virtual-machines/v1_9/\nFor all Virtual Machines that have two or more instances deployed across two or more Availability Zones in the same Azure region,\nwe guarantee you will have Virtual Machine Connectivity to at least one instance at least 99.99% of the time.\nzellck\nzellck\n\n7 months, 2 weeks ago\nAn Azure Service Level Agreement (SLA) is a commitment by Microsoft to provide a certain level of service availability for a\nspecific Azure service. The SLA for virtual machines guarantees a certain level of uptime for the virtual machine instance.\nSpecifically, it guarantees at least 99.95% availability per month for virtual machines running on a single instance, and 99.99%\navailability per month for virtual machines running on two or more instances.\nClaireMK\nClaireMK\n\n8 months ago\nThey Guarantee uptime https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/support/legal/sla/virtual-machines/v1_9/\nLeShen\nLeShen\n\n8 months, 3 weeks ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nhttps://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/support/legal/sla/\nLK009\nLK009\n\n9 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nB\nIts Feature Availability.\nhttps://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/support/legal/sla/virtual-machines/v1_9/\nIt was there in MS practice exam\nCaptExam\nCaptExam\n\n4 months ago\nNo, it's uptime. It says so in the first line of the webpage you're referring to:\n\"The Service Level Agreements (SLA) describe Microsoft’s commitments",
