    "answerText": "Correct Answer:\n\nBox 1: No -\nMost services go to private preview then public preview before being released to general availability.\nThe private preview is\nonly available to certain Azure customers for evaluation purposes.\nBox 2: Yes -\nPublic Preview means that the service is in public beta and can be tried out by anyone with an Azure subscription. Services\nin public preview are often offered at a discount price.\nPublic previews are excluded from SLAs and in some cases, no support is offered.\nBox 3: No -\nAn Azure service in general availability is available to all Azure customers, not just a subset of the customers.\nReference:\nhttps://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/support/legal/preview-supplemental-terms/",
    "comments": "awron_durat\nawron_durat\n\n3 years, 4 months ago\nCorrect.\nHazemnz\nHazemnz\n\n2 years, 11 months ago\nNo - \"1. Private preview – during this phase we invite a few customers to take part in early access to new concepts and features.\n\"\nYes - \"2. Public preview – during this phase we allow any customer with the proper Azure AD license to evaluate the new\nfeature. \" Maybe this question can be evaluated as NO as it is stating \"ny customer with the proper Azure AD license\" needs to\nbe confirmed !\nNo - \"3. Generally available (GA) – After the public preview is completed, the feature is open for any licensed customer to use\"\nUrpiano\nUrpiano\n\n2 years, 7 months ago\nIMHO second should be YES. How can I use a public preview if my license doesn't include a requirement for the new feature?\nBut it's not restricted to a selected customers group, so is general available.\nmaaten\nmaaten\n\n2 years, 3 months ago\nIMHO you are wrong.\nWHATERH2O\nWHATERH2O\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nLMAOOO\nzellck\nzellck\n\n7 months, 2 weeks ago\nNYN is the answer.\nAjaykrish\nAjaykrish\n\n1 year, 8 months ago\ngot it on 29-Nov-2021\n\nJason71\nJason71\n\n1 year, 10 months ago\nGot this on the 19/10/2021 exam!\nSarahxx\nSarahxx\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nappeared 18th July 2021\nJimmyYop\nJimmyYop\n\n2 years, 2 months ago\nAppeared in 21 - Jun -21 Exam\ngrimpy\ngrimpy\n\n2 years, 2 months ago\n3=Yes. Amazon DevOps is in GA, but not available for free tier customers.\nmpooja\nmpooja\n\n2 years, 2 months ago\nAppeared in 05 - Jun -21 Exam\ntaoj\ntaoj\n\n2 years, 2 months ago\nGot it on 01 Jun 2021\nGerardo1971\nGerardo1971\n\n2 years, 3 months ago\nCorrect answer\ncarca91\ncarca91\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nNo-Yes-No\nhlacoucou\nhlacoucou\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nI had this question in the exam 19/04/2021\nAzurite\nAzurite\n\n2 years, 7 months ago\nSorry the ? on the exam is for public",
