    "questionZh": "熱點 -\n對於以下每個陳述，如果該陳述為真，請選擇「是」。否則，選擇否。\n注意：每個正確的選擇都值得一分。\n熱門區域：",
    "answerTextZh": "Box 1: 是 -\nA reservation is where you commit to pay for a resource (for example a 虛擬機器) for one or three years. This gives\nyou a discounted price on the resource for the reservation period.\nBox 2: 否 -\nThere are other factors that influence the cost of a 虛擬機器 such as the virtual hard disks attached to the virtual\nmachine. You could have multiple 虛擬機器 with the same 'size' (B2S in this case) but with different virtual hard disk\nconfigurations.\nBox 3: 是 -\nWhen a 虛擬機器 is stopped (deallocated), the 虛擬機器 is unloaded/dismounted from the physical server in\nAzure. In this state, you are not charged for the 虛擬機器 itself.\nHowever, you are still charged for the storage costs of\nthe virtual hard disks attached to the 虛擬機器.\nIf the 虛擬機器 is stopped but not deallocated (this happens if you shut down the 虛擬機器 from the operating\n\nIf the 虛擬機器 is stopped but not deallocated (this happens if you shut down the 虛擬機器 from the operating\nsystem of the 虛擬機器), the 虛擬機器 is still mounted on the physical server in Azure and you are charged for\nthe 虛擬機器 itself as well as the storage costs.\nTo ensure that a 虛擬機器 is 'stopped (deallocated)', you need\nto stop the 虛擬機器 in the Azure portal.\n參考資料:\nhttps://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/reservations/\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/linux/b-series-burstable\nhttps://blogs.technet.microsoft.com/uspartner_ts2team/2014/10/10/azure-virtual-machines-stopping-versus-stopping-\ndeallocating/"
