    "comments": "namco23\nnamco23\n\n4 years, 3 months ago\nThere should be a moderator to delete the leftover comments that do not help anyone other than to confuse\nDBoss\nDBoss\n\n5 years, 2 months ago\nCommunity vote distribution\nB (100%)\n\nAnswer is B, as Network Interface are not charged. See Azure pricing calculator https://azure.microsoft.com/en-\nin/pricing/calculator/\nAcheshS\nAcheshS\n\n4 years, 2 months ago\nit doesnt have network interfaces in it?\nwendyy\nwendyy\n\n3 years, 5 months ago\nVirtual Network in Azure is free of charge. Every subscription is allowed to create up to 50 Virtual Networks across all regions. In\nthis price page, in netwroking, there is no item called Netwrok interface, so it is free.\nmsmt\nmsmt\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\non the exam on 29jun2023\nMarcal\nMarcal\n\n1 year, 9 months ago\nYes, removing the unused network interfaces can help reduce Azure costs for the company. Network interfaces are charged\nbased on the number of hours they exist, regardless of their association with a virtual machine. So removing unused network\ninterfaces can help reduce costs.\nSo the correct answer to your question is A. Yes.\nNoursBear\nNoursBear\n\n4 months, 3 weeks ago\nunbelievable\nzellck\nzellck\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nSelected Answer:\nB\nB is the answer.\nRaja8080\nRaja8080\n\n2 years, 3 months ago\nPublic IP Addresses are charged so yes the answer is B\nTonyghostR05\nTonyghostR05\n\n2 years, 4 months ago\nCorrect Ans is Remove Public IP\nTherefore, this is B\ndkiaidoo\ndkiaidoo\n\n3 years, 1 month ago\nAnswer should be Yes, as IP cost (more details -> https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/ip-addresses/)\n[Removed]\n[Removed]\n\n2 years, 11 months ago\nread the question carefully. Solution -> you removed the NIC and does the removal of NIC reduce the cost to the firm?\nswapnasantoshi\nswapnasantoshi\n\n3 years, 2 m",
