    "comments": "Comments\nRezaparsa\nRezaparsa\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nThe answer is definitely wrong. it is Azure Active Directory.\nAAsif098\nAAsif098\n\n2 years, 1 month ago\nAgreed should be Azure AD\nSa_Msa\nSa_Msa\n\n1 year, 10 months ago\nNo it's correct, it should be Subscriptions.\nSee below from this link: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/partner-center/assign-azure-subscriptions\nAssign Azure subscriptions to your customers\nTo assign an Azure subscription to a customer, use the following steps:\nIn Partner Center, select Customers and then locate the customer you want to manage.\nSelect the down arrow at the end of the row to expand the customer's record and then select Microsoft Azure Management\nPortal.\nYou're directed to the Azure portal where you can manage the customer's subscriptions.\nAt the Azure portal, select Subscriptions.\nSelect the subscription you want to assign and then select Access Control.\nSelect Add to add a user to the subscription.\nAfter you add the user to the subscription, you can assign the user a role and the account to which the user will have access.\nSuper63\nSuper63\n\n3 months, 3 weeks ago\nIn here shows how to \"assign\" which means that I assign to an already existent user. The question is about creating a user, not\nassigning a subscription to an existent user\nrteinformatica\nrteinformatica\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\nThe answer is Azure Active Directory.\nWhy? Because it says you have to CREATE a new user. From Subscriptions, you can associate a previously created user, but it\ndoes not allow you to create a new one.\nThat's the difference...\nDmarcetic\nDmarcetic\n\n1 week, 6 days ago\nThe question is not how to create user in Azure. The question is how to create a new user for an Azure subscription and the\nanswer is Subscription as explained in https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/pa",
