    "comments": "Super63\nSuper63\n\n3 months, 3 weeks ago\nTo begin with we can eliminate A and D as a VM is neither a storage nor an application. It is a resource\nSo we place resources in resource groups regardles of the administrative unit\nBy the way: An administrative unit in Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) is a resource that can act as a container for other Azure\nAD resources. It can contain only users, groups, or devices. Purpose: Administrative units are designed to restrict permissions in\na role to specific portions of an organization.\nSo this is not pertinent to the question as a VM cvan be place in a number of administrative untits depending on the scenario\nRon256\nRon256\n\n11 months, 1 week ago\nOn the exam:\nSeveral questions were on the exam. Scored 905 on 03/16/2024.\nAndySmith\nAndySmith\n\n1 year, 2 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nB\nin \"Resource Group\". All other options are irrelevant to the context of the Q.\nCommunity vote distribution\nB (100%)\n\nsohal999999999999\nsohal999999999999\n\n1 year, 3 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nB\ncorrect",
