    "comments": "Super63\nSuper63\n\n3 months, 3 weeks ago\n1) In the lift-and-shift approach to cloud migration, applications, systems, workloads, and data are moved from on-premises to the\ncloud with little or no changes. Resources hosted in the data center are copied and \"lifted\" from the on-premises infrastructure.\n2) Lift-and-shift – also known as rehosting – is a migration strategy that involves moving data and applications from an on-\npremises location to Azure-based virtual machines in the cloud. It's a popular approach, mainly because it is relatively quick and\npainless.\nSince it involves Virtual Machines, they need to be lifted-and-shifted to IaaS\njambroba\njambroba\n\n7 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\n- A. infrastructure as a service (IaaS)\nMikalai271\nMikalai271\n\n7 months, 2 weeks ago\nThis question was in my exam on July 3, 2024.\nTestTaker09876\nTestTaker09876\n\n10 months, 2 weeks ago\nLift and shift is one of top advertised features of infrastructure as service\nCommunity vote distribution\nA (100%)\n\nhttps://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/resources/cloud-computing-dictionary/what-is-iaas\nPayu1994\nPayu1994\n\n10 months, 3 weeks ago\nA it is.",
