    "comments": "zimzimzimma\nzimzimzimma\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\n'High Availability' is correct.\nNoursBear\nNoursBear\n\n6 months, 3 weeks ago\n\"Reliability\" is not part of the MS cloud computing vocabulary\nd33f59e\nd33f59e\n\n7 months ago\nReliability is the ability of a system to recover from failures and continue to function. It's also one of the pillars of the Microsoft\nAzure Well-Architected Framework.\nTestTaker09876\nTestTaker09876\n\n10 months, 2 weeks ago\n\nAvailability refers to system uptime, or when the system is available to users/other applications. High Availability simply means that\nsystem is designed to run for a very long period of time. So in the context of this question, if a service failure were to happen you\ncan give cloud resources via high availability to prevent mission critical applications from failing.",
