    "comments": "zimzimzimma\nzimzimzimma\n\n1 year, 7 months ago\n'A. APIs' is correct.\nKey is Desktop Applications which need to interact with Azure resources in a programmatical way, so APIs.\nsimon9251\nsimon9251\n\n1 year, 5 months ago\nThis question was on my exam today. 8/31/2023\nMoeA\nMoeA\n\n1 year, 4 months ago\nDid you see other questions from here on the test? Can you please give examples if you did see any similar questions?\nZakirh\nZakirh\n\n2 months, 4 weeks ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\n'A. APIs' is correct.\nSuper63\nSuper63\n\n3 months, 3 weeks ago\nANSWER: A\nC& D are out as thet are run by people, not by desktop applications. A desktop application does not decide which scrip to use,\nCommunity vote distribution\nA (50%)\nB (50%)\n\nC& D are out as thet are run by people, not by desktop applications. A desktop application does not decide which scrip to use,\npeople do.\nA- Correct-The underlying purpose of APIs is always the same: to let one piece of software communicate with another.\nB-Incorrect-ARM template - A JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) file that defines one or more resources to deploy to a resource\ngroup, subscription, management group, or tenant.\nC-Incorrect-The Azure command-line interface (Azure CLI) is a set of commands used to create and manage Azure resources.\nThe Azure CLI is available across Azure services and is designed to get you working quickly with Azure, with an emphasis on\nautomation.\nD-The Azure Cloud Shell allows connectivity to Microsoft Azure using an authenticated, browser-based shell experience that’s\nhosted in the cloud and accessible from virtually anywhere as long as you have access to your favourite browser\nDixonDavis\nDixonDavis\n\n4 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nA\nThe question talks about an application so its a program and need to connect programatically\nlara400\nlara400",
