    "comments": "jbzeh\njbzeh\n\n11 months ago\noups... last question ! exam in deux days ! i'll come with feedback!\nmanusha96\nmanusha96\n\n2 weeks, 6 days ago\nC & E\nThe configuration and maintenance of storage (A) typically fall under the customer's responsibilities. This is because IaaS provides\nthe basic building blocks, and customers have the flexibility to configure and manage their storage solutions according to their\nspecific needs.\nCSP provides the storage infrastructure, the customer manages how it is configured and used\nTridi\nTridi\n\n1 month, 1 week ago\nSelected Answer:\nAE\nIn the Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) model:\nThe cloud service provider is responsible for managing and maintaining the infrastructure layer, including hardware, networking,\nCommunity vote distribution\nAE (50%)\nCE (50%)\n\nThe cloud service provider is responsible for managing and maintaining the infrastructure layer, including hardware, networking,\nstorage, and the physical security of the datacenter.\nThe customer is responsible for managing higher layers such as the operating system, applications, and data.\nEhCloudGrrrU\nEhCloudGrrrU\n\n3 months ago\nSelected Answer:\nCE\nC and E - pretty obvious.\nPayu1994\nPayu1994\n\n4 months, 3 weeks ago\nI think B & C\n[Removed]\n[Removed]\n\n10 months, 3 weeks ago\nLast question... exam friday next week. Will re-read all questions at least once, cross your fingers for me :)\nIlyassbouichi\nIlyassbouichi\n\n11 months ago\nCorrect",
